A grid formatted under the shrink-to-fit max-content constraint, whose auto inline size and every ancestor's up
to the constraint root stretch from its stand-in width, counts automatic repetitions from an indefinite size (CSS
Grid 7.2.3.2): the tracks repeat once, or as the grid's min and max widths ask. Nested grid items no longer add the
stand-in width level by level into hundreds of tracks.

